<title>UK: BA shares down as ground staff back strike.</title>
<headline>BA shares down as ground staff back strike.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in British Airways Plc traded lower on Monday after a majority of the company's ground staff backed strike action in protest over BA's plans to sell its catering unit.</p>
<p>BA shares were 10.5p lower at 685p at 1435 GMT, after the Transport and General Workers Union said 62.5 percent of ground staff balloted had voted for a strike.  </p>
<p>The vote increases the likelihood of disruption to BA flights during the peak summer period. BA cabin crew last week voted in favour of a strike in a separate ballot last week.</p>
<p>The two ballots stem from different issues but both are linked to BA's cost-cutting measures aimed at saving one billion stg by 2000 and seem likely to lead to coordinated industrial action.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
